~ PLMENUS.STR   31 May 1985
~
~ Message strings are organized into categories: header messages, label 
~ messages, etc.  The start of a message category in this file is defined by 
~ a '$', a number of dashes, four significant characters, optional 
~ characters, and a newline.  Categories may appear in any order, but a 
~ given category may appear only once. 
~
~ Each message within a category has a number associated with it.  Numbers 
~ start with zero for the first message and run consecutively.  Messages are 
~ terminated by a '%' character.
~
~ The '\' character causes the display to be cleared.
~
~ Lines beginning with '~' are comments here and have no effect.
~
~ Non-printing characters (i.e. form feeds) in this file are ignored.
